network-manager-openvpn3 (0.6.0~alpha.2-1~dhcargo1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Security & correctness hardening sweep across all five crates
    (audit follow-up):
    - service: O_NONBLOCK on the profile open (FIFO can't stall the
      daemon); allow-list KEY_EXTRA_ROUTES so a crafted vpn.data can't
      inject openvpn directives past the security tail; serialize
      Connect; suppress spurious Failure on NM-initiated Disconnect.
    - properties: harden the export-side pinned-profile read
      (O_NOFOLLOW + size cap) to match import; NULL-check
      g_module_error()/dli_fname; wrap every extern "C" entrypoint in
      catch_unwind; fail closed on inline-blob writes when the secure
      cert dir is unavailable.
    - ovpn3-client: propagate UserInputQueueGetTypeGroup errors instead
      of masking auth failures as an empty queue.
    - editor/auth-dialog: catch_unwind at the FFI boundary; zeroize
      secret intermediates; O_NONBLOCK keyfile probe.

 -- Dominik Jarmulowicz <dominik.jarmulowicz@oversee.biz>  Thu, 28 May 2026 23:30:00 +0200

network-manager-openvpn3 (0.6.0~alpha.1-1~dhcargo1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Experimental dh-cargo packaging: resolves Rust deps from the
    Ubuntu / Debian archive's `librust-*-dev` packages (no vendored
    cargo tarball).  Workspace Cargo.toml downgraded on this branch to
    match the GTK4 / libadwaita / glib / if-addrs versions noble ships.
  * Version suffix `~dhcargo1` keeps these .deb's distinguishable from
    the vendored layout's builds (`-1`) when both layouts produce
    output side-by-side; apt orders `-1~dhcargo1` strictly below `-1`.

 -- Dominik Jarmulowicz <dominik.jarmulowicz@oversee.biz>  Sun, 24 May 2026 15:00:00 +0200

network-manager-openvpn3 (0.6.0~alpha.1-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Initial Ubuntu PPA packaging of the Rust-port nm-openvpn3 plugin.
  * Package names follow the Debian `network-manager-<vpn>` convention
    used by network-manager-openvpn, -pptp, -vpnc, -strongswan, etc.
    Runtime identifiers (binary names, .name file, D-Bus service name)
    keep the upstream `nm-openvpn3` short form.
  * Two binary packages: network-manager-openvpn3 (service + auth-dialog,
    headless) and network-manager-openvpn3-gnome (libnm + GTK4 editor
    cdylibs, locale, AppStream metainfo).
  * Vendored cargo dependencies shipped via orig-vendor component
    tarball; the build runs `cargo --offline --locked` so Launchpad
    builders never reach crates.io.

 -- Dominik Jarmulowicz <dominik.jarmulowicz@oversee.biz>  Sat, 23 May 2026 14:30:00 +0200
